he character conjures forward, it cannot carry a value higher than what could be purchased with Resources 3. </div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Either Space (3?) to get an actual item, or Prime 3 for Platonic Form.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1079756-copycat-mages?p=1079772#post1079772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hidden Reality (4 dot contract)<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The character changes some feature of her surrounding that was not previously obvious and so might have been present naturally. For example, she may create a hidden latch on a box to allow her to open it, a wall outlet behind a table, or a window or door behind a curtain. In all cases, the change must be reasonable and relatively minor in scope. A new door in a wall must lead to the other side of the wall, and not to the outside. Anything she creates or changes must be considered a part of an object, such as a lock on a door, a door in a room, or a window to a car. All changes vanish after one scene or if no one is paying attention to it.<br /> Wizened characters may create objects that could reasonably be found in a room or building, as long as she cannot see into the room or building she is performing this Contract in. She may find a set of keys on a nearby table, or a car parked in the garage.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Depends more on what is being done, than how, but I'd say Matter (of various ratings) could cover it. And ignore the &quot;must not know what is in the room&quot; restriction.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T08:34:27-07:00","id":1079804,"title":"","content":"To take the biggest one I can- how would a mage replicate the Utterance that makes meteors rain down over several miles (away from books, don't know the name off hand).<br /> <br /> Also, how can a mage replicate &quot;able to use my powers in a nightclub without the spell decaying and Cuthlhu eating me&quot; haha sick burn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T08:40:12-07:00","id":1079806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urbenmyth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1079756-copycat-mages?p=1079804#post1079804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To take the biggest one I can- how would a mage replicate the Utterance that makes meteors rain down over several miles (away from books, don't know the name off hand).<br /> <br /> Also, how can a mage replicate &amp;quot;able to use my powers in a nightclub without the spell decaying and Cuthlhu eating me&amp;quot; haha sick burn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Meteors, sympathetic use of Matter 5.<br /> <br /> Mages can use their powers anywhere no matter how packed with Sleepers if the results of those powers won't be obvious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T08:43:41-07:00","id":1079810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urbenmyth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1079756-copycat-mages?p=1079804#post1079804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To take the biggest one I can- how would a mage replicate the Utterance that makes meteors rain down over several miles (away from books, don't know the name off hand).<br /> <br /> Also, how can a mage replicate &quot;able to use my powers in a nightclub without the spell decaying and Cuthlhu eating me&quot; haha sick burn.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm thinking either some heavy Fate usage (for altering existing trajectories), or some Matter 5 (Making) cast at orbit, and maybe given a Forces shove.<br /> <br /> For the later, just keep the magic use subtle - it doesn't provoke Dissonance if people don't realize magic is going on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T09:47:15-07:00","id":1079839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urbenmyth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1079756-copycat-mages?p=1079804#post1079804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To take the biggest one I can- how would a mage replicate the Utterance that makes meteors rain down over several miles (away from books, don't know the name off hand).<br /> <br /> Also, how can a mage replicate &quot;able to use my powers in a nightclub without the spell decaying and Cuthlhu eating me&quot; haha sick burn.</div> </div> </div> </div>The previous answers work quite nicely, I'll try for a low-powered alternative.<br /> <br /> The &quot;over several miles&quot; part thing is just about scale and range, but meteor strike? I have been wondering what a Fate 3 direct damage spell could look like. And there you go. Meteor strike, Fate 3, 1 bashing damage per Potency, as small meteorites that are falling all the time just happen to fall in the right direction. Generally they burn out in their atmospheric entry, but some sometimes survive, small though they be.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, Fate 3 version of the Forces 3 spell Call Lightning, Call Meteor - same thing, only during a meteor shower, not a storm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","name":"Aeryes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11842_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T09:49:57-07:00","id":1079843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeryes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1079756-copycat-mages?p=1079839#post1079839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;over several miles&quot; part thing is just about scale and range</div> </div> </div> </div>This is probably one of the bigger limiters, as area of effect doesn't go over 'A campus, or a small neighborhood' in size.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T10:34:23-07:00","id":1079864,"title":"","content":"Let's start with the basics.<br /> <br /> How you would copy the passive powers each splat has?<br /> <br /> Vampire: Downgrade lethal dmg, has a bite attack that can harm or cause pleasure, addictive and healing blood.<br /> Werewolf: Enhanced senses, 5 different forms, can Reach and talk to spirits.<br /> Changeling: Can seal Oaths, has a Kith and a Mien(and a Mask to not be detected as inhuman), can enter the Hedge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T10:59:19-07:00","id":1079871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1079756-copycat-mages?p=1079864#post1079864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampire:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Downgrade lethal dmg,</li> <li>has a bite attack that can harm or cause pleasure,</li> <li>addictive and</li> <li>healing blood.</li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> 1. Death Shielding (Death armor already does this)<br /> 2. Life 3 for the Bite, Mind for the induced emotion/sensation<br /> 3. Mind for addiction. Maybe Matter to turn saliva into a drug.<br /> 4. Life 3 for healing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1079756-copycat-mages?p=1079864#post1079864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolf: Enhanced senses, 5 different forms, can Reach and talk to spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Life (maybe Forces)<br /> 2. Life 3-4<br /> 3. Spirit Arcana<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1079756-copycat-mages?p=1079864#post1079864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changeling: Can seal Oaths, has a Kith and a Mien(and a Mask to not be detected as inhuman), can enter the Hedge.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Fate<br /> 2. ???<br /> 3. Mind for mental illusion, maybe Prime (or a mix of the two)<br /> 4. Fate 5 has been said to make Hedge Gates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-17-2017, 02:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T11:21:25-07:00","id":1079892,"title":"","content":"Various levels of life for kith? You could probably replicate the appearence and most kith blessings with some kind of shapeshifiting. Maybe forces or matter for more esoteric ones but it should be doable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T11:25:49-07:00","id":1079895,"title":"","content":"Hehehehe. Impossible Spoor from Werewolf 2nd Edition. I looove that power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T11:55:42-07:00","id":1079910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1079756-copycat-mages?p=1079895#post1079895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hehehehe. Impossible Spoor from Werewolf 2nd Edition. I looove that power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's see. Life 1 for Enhanced Senses with Reach for tracking.<br /> Add some Forces for tracking soundwaves and wi-fi signals.<br /> Time to ignore the penaltys due to the age of the trail.<br /> And, of course, Space, to get Sympathy and find the subject.<br /> <br /> This can also be done just with Space, but I wanted to use more arcanas for the flavor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T11:58:50-07:00","id":1079913,"title":"","content":"What about a Demonic Bargain? Say, I swap my memories of childhood for wealth and fame. How would a mage replicate that?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12109,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","user":"Urbenmyth","date":". 04-17-2017, 03:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T12:03:43-07:00","id":1079917,"title":"","content":"Oh no, wait, Miracle with +2 reach for the wealth and fame and Mind Wipe for the childhood memories. Solved my own problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T12:11:36-07:00","id":1079922,"title":"","content":"Beast 's Lairs? I guess it would involve some weird combination of Spirit, Mind and Space.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T18:00:20-07:00","id":1080106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1079756-copycat-mages?p=1079922#post1079922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beast 's Lairs? I guess it would involve some weird combination of Spirit, Mind and Space.</div> </div> </div> </div>this one's tricky, you'd need 3-5 Mind to manipulate the temenos into a lair (can you make a demesne in the temenos?) and then Space to be able to draw people into it, HOWEVER, i'm uncertain that a person can be physically drawn into the temenos by awakened magic. Now since beasts can do it that means it's Possible and thus doable but it may require some serious magic if it's not a normal thing that can be done with the astral plane, you'd probably need to combo of Mind (for the temenos) Space (for the abduction and the altered location) and Matter/Life (in order to make a place where physical matter can exist). as to the badass monstrous form that would be either Life 3-5 (depending on how badass we're talking) or mind just Mind (if it's just your astral form). this becomes a great deal easier if a sanctum can be created in the astral plane but i'm not sure that's doable.<br /> <br /> Although if you're content inflicting psychic trauma just Mind [whatever] and Space 2 will be fine. actually i had the thought once of what a neat idea it would be if one beast tried to awaken another beast only for them to awaken as a mastigos mid hunt, i'd kind of like to see the effect on a beast who beheld pandemonium even if briefly<br /> <br /> Also remember that while mages are very powerful they can only maintain a few duration spells at a time safely without expending great resources or risking dangerous instability. So duplicating all these innate powers, while doable, would cut heavily into the number of spells they could otherwise use to protect themselves and their sanctums","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3729,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","user":"Darkfoxdev","date":". 04-17-2017, 09:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T18:07:38-07:00","id":1080109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkfoxdev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1079756-copycat-mages?p=1080106#post1080106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> this one's tricky, you'd need 3-5 Mind to manipulate the temenos into a lair (can you make a demesne in the temenos?) and then Space to be able to draw people into it, HOWEVER, i'm uncertain that a person can be physically drawn into the temenos by awakened magic. Now since beasts can do it that means it's Possible and thus doable but it may require some serious magic if it's not a normal thing that can be done with the astral plane, you'd probably need to combo of Mind (for the temenos) Space (for the abduction and the altered location) and Matter/Life (in order to make a place where physical matter can exist). as to the badass monstrous form that would be either Life 3-5 (depending on how badass we're talking) or mind just Mind (if it's just your astral form). this becomes a great deal easier if a sanctum can be created in the astral plane but i'm not sure that's doable.<br /> <br /> Also remember that while mages are very powerful they can only maintain a few duration spells at a time safely without expending great resources or risking dangerous instability. So duplicating all these innate powers, while doable, would cut heavily into the number of spells they could otherwise use to protect themselves and their sanctums</div> </div> </div> </div>A Sanctum or a Demesne ought to be doable in the Astral, a Mage's own Oneiros pretty much is a Demesne already in fact. Also, transporting someone's physical body to the Astral is possible, but comes with no upsides, which might be perfect if you're trying to emulate a Lair anyway (Not sure, only have a rudimentary understanding of Beast). Mind 4 +Life 4 should be able to convert you into a Mind compatible ephemeral form, from there Space should be able to teleport you or someone else into the Astral, though you may be able to cut out the Space bit if you use an Astral Verge or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T02:19:48-07:00","id":1080222,"title":"","content":"If you find an Astral Verge you could skip also Life and navigate there with some Mind 1 or Space 1. It will translate you without the need of magic but the thread is about using it so this solution is not working for it. <br /> After Patterning yourself with Life and Mind you should be able to meditate yourself entirely into Astral without the need of Space. Or use a spell to insert yourself into your own Oneiros. But honestly you could grant yourself just <i>properties </i>of Goetia and enter Astral with Mind/Life Weaving.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T05:14:25-07:00","id":1080252,"title":"","content":"Basically everything a vampire can do can be replicated using Life or Mind. However, is there anything in the mage repertoire that can replicate the first three dots of Auspex?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T05:18:50-07:00","id":1080256,"title":"","content":"Moving away from playable powers, what about an idigam's Forge Herald?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T09:33:08-07:00","id":1080380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urbenmyth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1079756-copycat-mages?p=1080256#post1080256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moving away from playable powers, what about an idigam's Forge Herald?</div> </div> </div> </div>Forge Herald gives a lot of different, distinct powers. Spirit (maybe also needing Life) to give the target an essence pool/Numina, Space (and maybe Mind) to see through their eyes, and definitely Mind to communicate through your mind. Next up is essentially psychic domination or possession, both potentially needing Space for Sympathetic Range, and while you can't remove a werewolfs weakness to silver, you could just shield them from it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T13:33:55-07:00","id":1080524,"title":"","content":"I don't know if it's still true, but I remember back before Mage 2e came out Dave said that the &quot;Create Fetish&quot; spell in the book doesn't let you create fetishes from the Werewolf book, you're limited to just the spirit's influences. That doesn't mean you cant creative thaumaturgy a version that does get you non-influence based fetishes though.<br /> <br /> The most glaring limitation with Awakened magic that I've encountered is that you need archmastery to create magic that changes based on external stimuli. I'm pretty sure that there are things that are pretty easy to do with a computer program that either take the practice of dynamics or, possibly, an extravagantly trained entity created with mastery. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T13:46:46-07:00","id":1080531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solidork</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1079756-copycat-mages?p=1080524#post1080524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if it's still true, but I remember back before Mage 2e came out Dave said that the &quot;Create Fetish&quot; spell in the book doesn't let you create fetishes from the Werewolf book, you're limited to just the spirit's influences. That doesn't mean you cant creative thaumaturgy a version that does get you non-influence based fetishes though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Create Fetish has an ambiguous wording that implies that it -might- be possible to create a Fetish that has more powers than just Influence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T13:47:50-07:00","id":1080532,"title":"","content":"Spirit 's influences can do pretty much anything. Numinas are simply easier and cheaper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T14:52:23-07:00","id":1080568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1079756-copycat-mages?p=1080531#post1080531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Create Fetish has an ambiguous wording that implies that it -might- be possible to create a Fetish that has more powers than just Influence.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a very generous reading of the spell.<br /> <br /> 'Fetishes work like an Imbued Items, save that a fetish is powered by Essence and, instead of holding a Supernal spell, it holds one of the bound spirit\u2019s Influences and, possibly, some of its Numina.<br /> Creating a fetish requires that the spell have one Potency per dot of Influence the object will possess, plus one Potency per Numen.'<br /> <br /> It seems pretty clear you either get Influences, Numen, or both. Or an Essence battery, mentioned later.<br /> <br /> Back on topic.<br /> <br /> What about Hide the Curse? A mage becomes a completely ordinary human without access to supernatural powers, passive or active, for a day.<br /> <br /> Or Reconsolatio? Is there a way to pump a human's Integrity to 10 for the duration?<br /> <br /> Unholy Avatar? When you die, you reincarnate in the body of a previously-prepared child.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-18-2017, 06:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T15:06:07-07:00","id":1080575,"title":"","content":"It's pretty clear to me that you can split potency between Influences and Numina. I literally cannot find a reason for blocking something like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T15:10:45-07:00","id":1080578,"title":"","content":"Hide the Curse should be doable with prime 3 or 4 and targets consent.<br /> Reconsolation - maybe Mind(Death and Prime with a stretch)at 3 dots?<br /> Unholy Avatar is a Death 4 effect for me. In 1e you could trade your death for someones life.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T01:57:22-07:00","id":1080788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solidork</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1079756-copycat-mages?p=1080524#post1080524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The most glaring limitation with Awakened magic that I've encountered is that you need archmastery to create magic that changes based on external stimuli. I'm pretty sure that there are things that are pretty easy to do with a computer program that either take the practice of dynamics or, possibly, an extravagantly trained entity created with mastery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, look at that. It seems like the Free Council does have a point.<br /> <br /> Hide the Curse could also be done with Time - pull an alternate present version of the target which never got supernatural powers in the first place.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T23:22:39-07:00","id":1084356,"title":"","content":"Could a Mage use Shapechange(Life 4) to change into the various werewolf forms (Gauru, Urshul etc.) with all of its benefits and drawbacks?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T01:51:37-07:00","id":1084385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1079756-copycat-mages?p=1084356#post1084356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could a Mage use Shapechange(Life 4) to change into the various werewolf forms (Gauru, Urshul etc.) with all of its benefits and drawbacks?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just Shapechange? No. There are effects (like Lunacy) that would require other arcana to mimic. Pretty much all the effects <i>can</i> be imitated, but you're definitely going to need more than a single spell from a single arcanum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T03:40:14-07:00","id":1084400,"title":"","content":"Mages can turn into a purely physical Gauru form with Life 4. Patternig gives you broad strokes like 'get x in all of listed factors equal to potency' and those factors could be initiative, size, strength, claws, etc. so it would be one spell. Even weakness to silver can be replicated with Life, 3rd dot should do. Primal Fear that forces every every opponent to use Down&amp;Dirty Combat might be a Life Ruling spell that acts on instincts. You can replicate Lunacy with Life too. At least Atavism and Delusion conditions.<br /> The hardest aspect to achieve is regeneration of all bashing and lethal damage each turn. It's not worth it. For a mage its better to prevent than heal and armor of 10+ prevents very nicely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}